    "background": "Collected from Oberwolfach Reports, which document mathematical workshops and their open-problem discussions.\n\n**Source report:** [Real Algebraic Geometry with a View Toward Hyperbolic Programming and Free Probability (2021), Oberwolfach Reports, DOI 10.4171/owr/2020/12, pp. 639--712](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/12)\n\n## Literature review (checked 2026-08-22)\n\n**Status:** partially solved\n\n**Assessment.** The existence part is solved affirmatively by the Chebyshev morphism, which has only real periodic points. The question whether the corresponding locus has nonempty interior or full dimension remains open; only lower-dimensional families are known.\n\n**Sources checked.**\n\n- [Kozhasov--Kummer (2020)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2004.10003)\n- [Oberwolfach Report 12/2020](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2020/12)\n\nThis is a dated literature triage derived from the supplied OWR curation; verify time-sensitive status and cited claims independently.",
